Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET: free memory on the PS5 comes from the front (the pool's largest free block)

T94, shader set run B: "Shader set: free memory is unknown on this platform; nothing extracted".
The PS5 kernel has no vm.stats.vm.v_free_count sysctl. FreeMemoryBytes now first asks the front's
eden_free_memory_bytes (headless/performance.cpp: the largest free block of the direct memory
pool, the measure the caches there use), a weak symbol that other platforms do not have.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp b/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp
index e303bc2..c356172 100644
--- a/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/shader_set.cpp
@@ -284,7 +284,19 @@ std::vector<u8> Hydrate(const Facts& f, const Lowered& p) {
 }
 } // namespace
 
+} // namespace VideoCommon::ShaderSet
+// The PS5 front's answer (headless/performance.cpp): the largest free block of the pool the CPU
+// shares with the GPU, which is what the caches there measure memory by. The PS5 kernel has no
+// vm.stats counters (T94, run B: "free memory is unknown on this platform; nothing extracted").
+extern "C" unsigned long long eden_free_memory_bytes(void) __attribute__((weak));
+namespace VideoCommon::ShaderSet {
+
 u64 FreeMemoryBytes() {
+    if (eden_free_memory_bytes != nullptr) {
+        if (const u64 bytes = eden_free_memory_bytes(); bytes != 0) {
+            return bytes;
+        }
+    }
 #if defined(__linux__)
     struct sysinfo info {};
     if (sysinfo(&info) == 0) {
